  "source_findings": [
    "HostJoinScreen uses an enabled-unless-busy, single-line OutlinedTextField with raw displayName and a direct setDisplayName callback. Explicit focus clearing occurs only on submit or accepted Done action.",
    "setDisplayName synchronously stores value.take(128), including blank values; normalizedName is used for saved settings separately and does not overwrite the raw field value.",
    "The test waits for existence, taps once, reads the accessibility value, sends that many deletes in one typeText call, types Native Host in a second call, then immediately asserts its accessibility value. It does not record the post-delete value, a keyboard checkpoint, or a first-responder checkpoint.",
    "Compose assigns the TextView accessibility trait to EditableText semantic nodes and adds its editing trait only for Focused semantics; the logged TextView type alone does not identify a UIKit class or establish keyboard focus.",
    "Compose accessibility value uses nonblank EditableText, then a semantic Text fallback. A future clear-value check must not assume blank edits always expose an empty String.",
    "The legacy editing chain synchronously applies EditProcessor commands, updates its input-service state, and forwards the app callback; the iOS input connection invokes editText, updateView, and then stateSnapshot in that order. This does not establish when pixels or the accessibility snapshot become current."
  ],
  "cause_limit": "Current source and text log establish failed observed name replacement. They do not determine missed key delivery, focus/session loss, stale AX value, or a persistent product defect. No production change is justified solely by these reads.",
